# System Files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Temporary files
tmp/
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# Agent Specific Files
# Generated agent adapter directories. These are derived artifacts regenerated
# from .sdd/, so they are not committed. AGENTS.md is the deliberate exception:
# it is the committed, cross-vendor baseline entrypoint.
.agents/
.claude/
.gemini/
.github/skills/
.gemini/skills/
graphify-out/

# ==============================================================================
# In-flight SDD specs (private working state)
# ==============================================================================
# Working phases are NOT published. `active/` and `backlog/` hold in-progress
# planning that contributors to the public repo should not read.
#
# Deliberately still tracked, because they are product documentation:
#   .sdd/specs/archive/       completed phases (the historical record)
#   defaults/specs-example/   the reference spec shipped to consumers
#
# The `/*` + `!.gitkeep` form is required. Git does not descend into a fully
# excluded directory, so `.sdd/specs/active/` on its own would make the
# negation unreachable and the directory would disappear on clone. doctor.sh
# checks that both directories exist.
.sdd/specs/active/*
!.sdd/specs/active/.gitkeep
.sdd/specs/backlog/*
!.sdd/specs/backlog/.gitkeep

# Per-developer sprint state. Machine-generated by phase.sh, references the
# in-flight phase, and differs per checkout. Regenerated on `phase.sh start`,
# or migrated from active-context.md on first use.
.sdd/state
